   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>noticed this in help page of unmarkedFramePCount:</div><div><br></div><div>y       An RxJ matrix of the repeated count data, where R is the number of sites...</div><div><br></div><div>siteCovs        A data.frame .... This should have M rows ...</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>So y has R rows for each site and siteCovs has M rows for each site.</div><div>So:</div><div><br></div><div>1) Is it a mistake and R = M?</div><div><br></div><div>Or,</div><div><br></div><div>2) Is it allowed to supply different amount of sites in siteCovs? For what?</div><div>For prediction?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>        Tomas</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
